"No edge. A breadth jump while the sector index is flat is usually a rebound inside a weak sector, not a coiled spring: such sectors broke out less often than normal (41% vs 56%) and did no better than the market. Results flipped between 2016-2020 (-1.4%) and 2021-2026 (+0.8%).", "verdict": "dropped", "data_to": "2026-11-23", "run_at": "2026-11-24T03:07"}, {"id": "E7", "title": "Delivery buying in lagging sectors", "question": "When a sector is lagging the market but its stocks see unusually heavy delivery buying, does it turn 'Improving' soon and do better afterwards?", "method": "Lagging = behind Nifty 500 over both 4 and 13 weeks. Delivery surge = the sector's 4-week average delivery % minus its prior 26-week average, in the top 20% of that sector's own history up to that week (no look-ahead). Compared with lagging weeks of low delivery (bottom half). Outcomes: turns Improving (4-week relative return positive) within 8 weeks; return vs Nifty 500 over the next 13 weeks.", "summary": "410 signals in 27 sectors. Turned Improving within 8 weeks 84% of the time vs 87% for lagging sectors with low delivery. Next 13 weeks vs Nifty 500: -0.4% (low-delivery comparison -1.1%).", "conclusion": "Weak and not reliable. Lagging sectors usually bounce within 8 weeks anyway (87%), so heavy delivery buying adds nothing to that. Over 13 weeks they lagged the market a little less (-0.4% vs -1.1%), but in 2016-2020 they still lagged by 1.3%. Not strong enough to use.", "verdict": "inconclusive", "data_to": "2026-11-23", "run_at": "2026-11-24T03:07"}, {"id": "E8", "title": "PSU banks vs private banks: who leads?", "question": "Do PSU bank stocks move first and private banks follow, or the other way round?", "method": "Nifty PSU Bank and Nifty Private Bank since 2016. (1) Correlation of one index's weekly move with the other's move 1-4 weeks later. (2) Whether last week's move of one improves the forecast of the other's next week (fit on 2016-2020, scored on 2021-2026). (3) Trend turns (price crossing its 50-day average after 20+ days) matched within 45 days: which turned first.", "summary": "Same-week correlation 0.66; lagged correlations are small (PSU\u2192private 1w +0.03, private\u2192PSU 1w +0.01). Adding the other index changed next-week direction accuracy by -0.6% (private) and -0.3% (PSU). Of 29 matched trend turns, PSU banks turned first 28% of the time (median -5 days). Leader: private banks.", "conclusion": "Private banks tend to turn first. In 29 matched trend turns since 2016, private banks crossed their 50-day average before PSU banks 72% of the time, by about 5 trading days (median). But week-to-week moves don't help predict each other (same-week correlation 0.66, lagged near zero). Useful as context, not as a trading signal; small sample.", "verdict": "kept (context only)", "data_to": "2026-11-23", "run_at": "2026-11-24T03:07"}], "notes": "Odds and history from NSE public data since 2015, not advice. Built by the NSE Pattern Atlas."}